1
00:00:00,050 --> 00:00:01,575
Which junction cools?

2
00:00:01,575 --> 00:00:11,614
The one where the current flows in the same direction it would through the hot junction of a Seebeck circuit of the same metals: for copper and iron, from copper to iron.

3
00:00:11,614 --> 00:00:18,333
That makes sense: a working thermocouple is a heat engine, taking in heat at its hot junction.

